## 6. RESTRICTIONS & COMPATIBILITY:
restrictions:
  max_io_current: "400mA"
  total_current_limit: "400mA"
  warnings[9]:
    - "FX5U-32MR/ES uses RELAY outputs (Y000-Y017) which CANNOT generate pulse train output (PTO) or PWM signals — relay switching time is ~10ms which makes it physically impossible to generate frequencies above ~50Hz; for applications requiring pulse output to stepper or servo drives (up to 200 kHz per axis) you MUST use the FX5U-32MT/ES (transistor output) variant; substituting relay for transistor in a motion application will cause all positioning instructions (PLSY, DRVA, DRVI) to fail or produce incorrect pulses"
    - "The built-in 24VDC service power supply output provides a maximum of 400mA for the FX5U-32MR/ES base unit — when FX5 extension modules are connected, each module draws additional current from this service supply, reducing the available current for external sensors; if the total load exceeds the service supply rating, output voltage drops, digital inputs are disabled, and ALL outputs turn off; always calculate the total service supply current budget before selecting extension modules"
    - "Do NOT apply external voltage to the [24+] and [24V] service power terminals on the CPU module — these terminals are outputs from the internal regulated supply; applying an external voltage to these terminals will damage the CPU module; some electronic loads with internal bias power supplies may inadvertently back-feed current into these terminals even when not intentionally powered externally"
    - "The FX5U-32MR/ES has NO dedicated USB programming port — the only permanent programming interface is the built-in Ethernet port (RJ45); direct USB programming is possible only via a GOT HMI transparent pass-through or via the optional FX5-485ADP adapter; always ensure the Ethernet connection is available before deploying to a machine without a screen"
    - "The built-in RS-485 port supports a maximum of 50m cable length — for longer distances or greater noise immunity, use the FX5-485ADP expansion board which also supports RS-485 but with improved common-mode rejection; install bus termination resistors (110Ω) at both physical ends of the RS-485 bus for cables longer than 10m; missing termination causes reflection and MODBUS CRC errors at higher baud rates"
    - "The 2 built-in analog inputs (AI ch1, AI ch2) and analog output (AO ch1) accept 0-10VDC ONLY — there is no built-in 4-20mA current input; to measure 4-20mA connect an external precision shunt resistor (500Ω) and measure the resulting 1-5VDC voltage; alternatively install a FX5-4AD or FX5-4AD-ADP expansion module which supports both voltage and current inputs with proper resolution; the built-in AI has no isolation from the CPU logic"
    - "The SD memory card slot must NOT be inserted or removed more than 500 times after first use — Mitsubishi Electric explicitly states this limit in the official hardware manual due to connector contact degradation; for high-frequency data logging applications that require frequent card swapping, this physical limit must be factored into the system maintenance plan; always power off the CPU before inserting or removing the SD card"
    - "The FX5U-32MR/ES power supply input is 100-240VAC (range 85-264VAC) — the /DS variant uses 24VDC; never connect a DC voltage source to the AC terminals of the /ES variant as this will destroy the input rectifier; verify the variant suffix before wiring; the terminal designations L, N on the /ES model accept AC only; a connection error will cause irreparable damage to the power supply section"
    - "The grounding requirement for the FX5U-32MR/ES is Class D (≤100Ω) using a wire of 2mm² or thicker connected to the FG (Functional Ground) terminal — do NOT share the FG ground with heavy electrical equipment, motors, or inverters as this introduces conducted noise that causes false input triggers and Ethernet communication errors; use a dedicated grounding conductor back to the main earth bar; incorrect or shared grounding is the most common cause of intermittent faults on MELSEC iQ-F systems"
compatibility:
  sw: "GX Works3 V1.000+ (primary — required for full FX5U features); GX Works2 (limited, no ST or advanced FB); MELSOFT Navigator; iQ Works; GX LogViewer for data logging"
  languages: "Ladder Diagram (LD);Structured Text (ST);Function Block Diagram (FBD/LD);Sequential Function Chart (SFC / MELSAP3)"
  frameworks: "IEC61131-3;SLMP;MC-protocol;MODBUS-TCP;MODBUS-RTU;CC-Link-IE-Field-Basic;MELSOFT;AnyWireASLINK-via-expansion;CC-Link-via-FX5-CL-LINK"
  certifications: "CE;UL;cUL;ATEX-Zone2-Class-I-Div2;KC;UKCA;RCM;EAC"

